    "problem_statement": "Middleware initialization fails with TypeError when using storage classes\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen initializing TinyDB with middleware that wraps storage classes, a TypeError is raised due to incorrect argument passing in the middleware initialization.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nfrom tinydb.storages import MemoryStorage, JSONStorage\nfrom tinydb.middlewares import CachingMiddleware\n\n# This fails with TypeError\ndb = TinyDB(storage=CachingMiddleware(MemoryStorage))\n\n# This also fails\ndb = TinyDB('test.db', storage=CachingMiddleware(JSONStorage))\n```\n\nThe error occurs when trying to create a TinyDB instance with any middleware that wraps a storage class. The TypeError indicates that the storage class constructor is being called with incorrect arguments.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe middleware should properly initialize the underlying storage and TinyDB should work normally with middleware-wrapped storage classes.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nA TypeError is raised during middleware initialization, preventing the database from being created."
